•our ability to attract and retain qualified employees and key personnel and further expand our overall headcount;

•our ability to develop relationships with service provider partners in order to expand internationally;

•our ability to stay abreast of new or modified laws and regulations, including executive orders, that currently apply or become applicable to our business both in the United States and internationally;

•our ability to maintain, protect and enhance our intellectual property;

•costs associated with defending intellectual property infringement and other claims; and

•other risks detailed below in Item 1A. "Risk Factors."

